[{:db/id 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" "question-5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192529 :question/problem "![](images/15/1562da3da10e26ab9b4aff6adaa71fcbb1c2de963b4bfc682663f7fcfa62f8d6.svg)\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\geq 3$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{\\infty} f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192754 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5cfff2a4-1c49-516b-a57f-2fc4f75675f3" "question-3576b4c9-6bad-5c07-bd64-6e08d7444e14"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" :question/id #uuid "7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-160446" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35e8275a-bb12-5f98-ba18-184bdee245ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35e8275a-bb12-5f98-ba18-184bdee245ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "35e8275a-bb12-5f98-ba18-184bdee245ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5d964b39-2482-5346-8612-8ce043b95788" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20a4da9c-5ad8-5dda-8ba1-be02f0af04f6" "answer-80eb078c-af7c-5800-a93c-6a0513121c1a" "answer-793d1056-34ae-50be-bbb1-25d45ceebdd3" "answer-5d964b39-2482-5346-8612-8ce043b95788" "answer-84482c4e-d104-578b-9bca-d5349bf9e6b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20a4da9c-5ad8-5dda-8ba1-be02f0af04f6" :answer/id #uuid "20a4da9c-5ad8-5dda-8ba1-be02f0af04f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80eb078c-af7c-5800-a93c-6a0513121c1a" :answer/id #uuid "80eb078c-af7c-5800-a93c-6a0513121c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-793d1056-34ae-50be-bbb1-25d45ceebdd3" :answer/id #uuid "793d1056-34ae-50be-bbb1-25d45ceebdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d964b39-2482-5346-8612-8ce043b95788" :answer/id #uuid "5d964b39-2482-5346-8612-8ce043b95788" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84482c4e-d104-578b-9bca-d5349bf9e6b4" :answer/id #uuid "84482c4e-d104-578b-9bca-d5349bf9e6b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0" :question/id #uuid "5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-160458" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3x-1},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)=3{e}^{3x-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{e}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x-1}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-0 \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-857db1a9-5baa-547f-ad7c-ffed08bafef2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-857db1a9-5baa-547f-ad7c-ffed08bafef2" :answer-field/id #uuid "857db1a9-5baa-547f-ad7c-ffed08bafef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76159088-6817-5983-996b-f9485affcb33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0345689f-fc2f-5460-9f38-e059246fb16f" "answer-4c86aada-f7d7-57c4-bae2-63a127ef9b11" "answer-76159088-6817-5983-996b-f9485affcb33" "answer-56eca2a0-0c43-50ef-b63f-0ce7a632d9be" "answer-0019d257-76eb-58eb-993a-0411c1c8ea5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0345689f-fc2f-5460-9f38-e059246fb16f" :answer/id #uuid "0345689f-fc2f-5460-9f38-e059246fb16f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c86aada-f7d7-57c4-bae2-63a127ef9b11" :answer/id #uuid "4c86aada-f7d7-57c4-bae2-63a127ef9b11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76159088-6817-5983-996b-f9485affcb33" :answer/id #uuid "76159088-6817-5983-996b-f9485affcb33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56eca2a0-0c43-50ef-b63f-0ce7a632d9be" :answer/id #uuid "56eca2a0-0c43-50ef-b63f-0ce7a632d9be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0019d257-76eb-58eb-993a-0411c1c8ea5a" :answer/id #uuid "0019d257-76eb-58eb-993a-0411c1c8ea5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278307 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}},\\, & x\\ge -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278310 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{3x+2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5cfff2a4-1c49-516b-a57f-2fc4f75675f3" :question/id #uuid "5cfff2a4-1c49-516b-a57f-2fc4f75675f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126017" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(6<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aad6b045-a52a-569f-a198-e336ad216b28"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aad6b045-a52a-569f-a198-e336ad216b28" :answer-field/id #uuid "aad6b045-a52a-569f-a198-e336ad216b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a01ed84-7ed4-5f6f-a73e-9bd30af3fabb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d012b452-3404-5413-b1e0-608d83d5420b" "answer-5a01ed84-7ed4-5f6f-a73e-9bd30af3fabb" "answer-81adb032-9089-5587-9426-36f061380efe" "answer-7acfc4ce-813f-5b26-908f-36ee952d848e" "answer-8fe28e04-3646-5d84-8159-6ca62c717e0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d012b452-3404-5413-b1e0-608d83d5420b" :answer/id #uuid "d012b452-3404-5413-b1e0-608d83d5420b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a01ed84-7ed4-5f6f-a73e-9bd30af3fabb" :answer/id #uuid "5a01ed84-7ed4-5f6f-a73e-9bd30af3fabb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81adb032-9089-5587-9426-36f061380efe" :answer/id #uuid "81adb032-9089-5587-9426-36f061380efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7acfc4ce-813f-5b26-908f-36ee952d848e" :answer/id #uuid "7acfc4ce-813f-5b26-908f-36ee952d848e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fe28e04-3646-5d84-8159-6ca62c717e0d" :answer/id #uuid "8fe28e04-3646-5d84-8159-6ca62c717e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3576b4c9-6bad-5c07-bd64-6e08d7444e14" :question/id #uuid "3576b4c9-6bad-5c07-bd64-6e08d7444e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-126021" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\le -4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\le -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -4) & =P(-\\infty <X\\le -4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}]}_{-\\infty }^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac73eb15-075e-5981-aef0-815786fcaa0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac73eb15-075e-5981-aef0-815786fcaa0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac73eb15-075e-5981-aef0-815786fcaa0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc72619e-93b0-55af-ae1f-db797a4bfb4f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc72619e-93b0-55af-ae1f-db797a4bfb4f" "answer-28421387-3618-5282-a14b-84e4566ab27b" "answer-dcc57884-296c-5280-8d50-e3fcc9ff86ad" "answer-06a255f8-64ef-51d8-a6e6-a071190bf006" "answer-23d2d105-cdbc-500b-881f-d9e0d158fa84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc72619e-93b0-55af-ae1f-db797a4bfb4f" :answer/id #uuid "fc72619e-93b0-55af-ae1f-db797a4bfb4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28421387-3618-5282-a14b-84e4566ab27b" :answer/id #uuid "28421387-3618-5282-a14b-84e4566ab27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcc57884-296c-5280-8d50-e3fcc9ff86ad" :answer/id #uuid "dcc57884-296c-5280-8d50-e3fcc9ff86ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/v